    "updated_at": "2015-12-14T15:57:26Z",
    "body": "My bad, then...\n\nOh, actually, close, but no cigar: in Chome and Safari, the value returned by the  `origin` getter is Punycode encoded too.\n\nDo I understand correctly that `URL.domainToUnicode()` is supposed to be a Punycode decoder? It doesn't seem to be implemented yet (Firefox, Safari, Chrome). There doesn't seem to be any native way to get the Unicode domain string in Safari and Chrome.\n\nIs the URL standard set in stone? If I understand correctly, it currently exposes to JS the as little transformations as possible for clean server interop, hence the lack of encoding of the `hash` part. I'd take consistent encoding over this any day...\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
