    "updated_at": "2015-12-14T16:02:42Z",
    "body": "> in Chome and Safari, the value returned by the origin getter is Punycode encoded too.\n\nOh wow, you might want to file issues for that against the specification. Perhaps we should change `origin`, but then `postMessage()` might need changes too. Ugh.\n\n`URL.domainToUnicode()` does more than just Punycode, since domains names use more than just Punycode, but it's close.\n\nThe URL standard is set in stone, modulo any outstanding issues and further implementation feedback.\n",
