    "body": "> Oh wow, you might want to file issues for that against the specification.\n\nWill do.\n\n> Perhaps we should change origin, but then postMessage() might need changes too. Ugh.\n\nI'm not familiar enough with these issues to have a meaningful opinion... \n\n> The URL standard is set in stone\n\nThat sucks a teeny bit for my use case (single page app router that has `'pathname'`, `'search'`, and `'hash'` modes), but since nobody follows the spec at the moment, I have to do feature detection live anyway.\n",
