    "updated_at": "2015-12-14T18:11:33Z",
    "body": "I'd prefer to have a consistent API, preferably Edge-like (however I guess it comes with other complications) but Safari-like would be nice too.\n\nRe. compatibility, see the table in my first post. I'd expect anyone serious about using it to do feature detection anyway, or, as it happens with the Mithril router (up to recently) to ignore the encoding differences and run into problems when chinese folks try to use it. Then you try to understand what's wrong with your regexps only to realize that the routes defined in code don't match those returned by the getters for encoding reasons.\n\nShould I also ping the MS folks for the lack of `/` in the `pathname` in IE11?\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
